[1m== 13. Punches so attendance and the hours export have something to say[0m
   SKIPPED. Adopt mode writes no SQL, and POST /workforce/pos/clock-events -- the only HTTP
   path to a punch -- needs a POS OPERATOR SESSION (register + operator + PIN + OD-2
   verification), which is a second product surface this seed does not stand up. So an
   adopted world carries NO clock punches: attendance shows planned minutes with no actuals,
   and the hours export has a header and no rows. That is the module's real boundary today.

